<tr id="S3.E9Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\hskip 18.49988pt\hskip 18.49988pt\rho\left\lVert\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}\hskip 18.49988pt\hskip 9.24994pt+\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})\right\rVert," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mo>‖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo><mo>‖</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\hskip 18.49988pt\hskip 18.49988pt\rho\left\lVert\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}\hskip 18.49988pt\hskip 9.24994pt+\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})\right\rVert,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Hessian matrix over the model weights using the validation set <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(V)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(V)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The final row in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) is the result of using the first-order Taylor expansion for <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}^{*}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}^{*}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), minimizing the first term of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{TOTAL}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{TOTAL}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is equivalent to minimizing the magnitude of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}+\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}+\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})</annotation></semantics></math>. It is worth noting that <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent from the calibration set <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> that we want to generate. The necessity condition for Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to be minimized is when <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})</annotation></semantics></math> have opposite directions, which is equivalent to optimize:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\arg\min_{X^{(T)}}cos(\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}},\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\arg\min_{X^{(T)}}cos(\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\delta_{\theta_{Q}},\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv\arg\max_{X^{(T)}}cos(\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)}),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv\arg\max_{X^{(T)}}cos(\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)}),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Estimating <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math> for the whole model can be very expensive, therefore, we turn to utilize the Hessian matrix <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Jacobian vector <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> of one layer <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> instead. As many quantization methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qian et al., 2023a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jeon et al., 2023</a>)</cite> usually keep the bit-width of the first convolutional layer and the last fully-connected layer higher than other layers in low-bit width setting  (e.g., in 2/2 setting, they are still kept at 8 bits while other layers are quantized to 2 bits), optimization based on the gradient of these two layers is likely to have more impact to the model’s performance. Therefore, we choose to use the fully-connected layer for our estimation, as it usually has a far higher number of parameters (more influence) than the first convolutional layer and its Jacobian matrix is easy to compute. For instance, for ResNet-18 architecture, the first convolutional layer has <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 7\times 7\times 3=9,408" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>9,408</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 7\times 7\times 3=9,408</annotation></semantics></math> parameters, while the last fully connected layer has <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512\times 1000=512,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>512,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512\times 1000=512,000</annotation></semantics></math> parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{(T)}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)},L-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{(T)}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)},L-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{(V)}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(V)},L-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{(V)}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(V)},L-1)</annotation></semantics></math> denote respectively input for the fully-connected layer of the training and validation sets with size <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times d</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of samples, and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weight matrix of the fully-connected layer with size <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times C</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of classes. We have:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)},L)=\mathcal{A}^{(T)}\mathcal{W}_{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.630em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.630em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)},L)=\mathcal{A}^{(T)}\mathcal{W}_{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(V)},L)=\mathcal{A}^{(V)}\mathcal{W}_{(L)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},X^{(V)},L)=\mathcal{A}^{(V)}\mathcal{W}_{(L)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.7" class="ltx_p">From Eq. (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), the Jacobian matrix w.r.t the fully connected layer can be easily estimated as:</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})_{(L)}=flatten\left({\mathcal{A}^{(T)}}^{T}g^{(T)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})_{(L)}=flatten\left({\mathcal{A}^{(T)}}^{T}g^{(T)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.8" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(T)}_{i}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},\mathbf{x}_{i},L)-\mathtt{f}(\theta_{FP},\mathbf{x}_{i},L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(T)}_{i}=\mathtt{f}(\theta_{Q},\mathbf{x}_{i},L)-\mathtt{f}(\theta_{FP},\mathbf{x}_{i},L)</annotation></semantics></math>. As the fully-connected layer is just a linear layer, the Hessian matrix <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> of this layer has the size <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dC\times dC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dC\times dC</annotation></semantics></math> and can be represented be:</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}&amp;0&amp;\dots&amp;0\\
0&{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}&amp;\dots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\dots&{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}&amp;0&amp;\dots&amp;0\\
0&amp;{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}&amp;\dots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\dots&amp;{\mathcal{A}^{(V)}}^{T}\mathcal{A}^{(V)}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.9" class="ltx_p">We can see that the Hessian matrix in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) has a positive diagonal, its diagonal elements are periodically overlapped and most of its off-diagonal elements are 0. Note that this matrix is independent of the training set <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> that we want to generate. Similar to AdaRound  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nagel et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, we assume that <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix with the same main diagonal value:</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}=cI," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{H}^{(\theta_{Q})}_{(L)}=cI,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.10" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is some constant, and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the identity matrix. Then (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) is equivalent to:</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\arg\max_{X^{(T)}}cos(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)}),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\arg\max_{X^{(T)}}cos(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)}),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(V)})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.11" class="ltx_p">As (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and the second term of <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{TOTAL}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{TOTAL}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) correlate, optimizing (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) will also partly optimize the second term in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Gradient matching without a validation set</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> SA zero-shot quantization.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Train</span>(<math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{FP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{FP}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{FP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{FP}</annotation></semantics></math>: The full-precision model.
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>: The generator. 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of images we want to generate. 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of warm-up iterations. 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of iterations for data optimization.
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of iterations for model quantization.

