              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
             Get the dataset <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}|\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}|\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{Q}=\theta_{Q}-\alpha_{\theta}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{R}(\theta_{Q},\theta_{FP},X^{(T)})}{\partial\theta_{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{Q}=\theta_{Q}-\alpha_{\theta}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{R}(\theta_{Q},\theta_{FP},X^{(T)})}{\partial\theta_{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">From (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), intuitively, we can see that the small set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> that we want to generate for calibration can decrease the SAM loss of the model over the validation set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(V)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(V)}</annotation></semantics></math> when the gradient of the model when evaluating on <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> matches with that when evaluating on <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(V)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(V)}</annotation></semantics></math>. In summary, there is a strong correlation between the minimization of the SAM loss and the matching of the gradients of the reconstruction loss <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{R}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{R}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated on the calibrated set and the validation set. Unfortunately, this objective is still hard to optimize because we do not have a large validation set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(V)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(V)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we propose a novel approach to approximate (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
Our idea is that if the training set is diverse enough,i.e., it spans over the data space, then for each sample <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that we want to generate, we just need to optimize its gradient to match with the gradients of samples in its neighborhood. In other word, we want to generate a training set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> such that samples of <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> are diverse and each sample of <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes the gradient matching with its neighbors.
To this end, we introduce an approach similar to SAM. We want to minimize the difference between the gradients of each generated sample and a sample in its neighbor with the highest gradient dissimilarity. Specifically, given a generated training set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}|\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}|\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> is a generator and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneqq\{\mathbf{z}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{|X^{(T)}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneqq\{\mathbf{z}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{|X^{(T)}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of embedding vectors to generate <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we want to estimate the perturbation <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}=\{\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{|X^{(T)}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}=\{\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{|X^{(T)}|}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}^{*}}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}^{*}}^{(T)}_{i}=\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample with the least similarity in gradient within the neighborhood of the original samples <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{(T)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}=\arg\max_{\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}=\arg\max_{\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{ s.t: }||\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}||\leq\nu," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">s.t: </mtext><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{ s.t: }||\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}||\leq\nu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> is a loss that measures the difference in gradients, assumed to be the cosine similarity distance. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foret et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, the closed-form solution for <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}=\nu\frac{\triangledown_{\mathbf{z}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})))}{\left\lVert\triangledown_{\mathbf{z}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})))\right\rVert}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}_{i}=\nu\frac{\triangledown_{\mathbf{z}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})))}{\left\lVert\triangledown_{\mathbf{z}_{i}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})))\right\rVert}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\mathcal{N})}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can estimate the sample that has its gradient matches with the gradients of its neighborhoods:</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}}\mathcal{L}_{GRAD}(\theta_{Q},\theta_{FP},X^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}}\mathcal{L}_{GRAD}(\theta_{Q},\theta_{FP},X^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon_{i}^{(\mathcal{N})})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\mathbf{z}_{i},\mathcal{G}}\mathcal{D}(\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i})),\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathcal{G}(\mathbf{z}_{i}+\epsilon_{i}^{(\mathcal{N})})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall i=1,2,..,|X^{(T)}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall i=1,2,..,|X^{(T)}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The above gradient matching loss will encourage (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) if the calibration set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math> is diverse enough.
Therefore, after normalizing <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(X^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math> to be unit vectors, we add a term to encourage the diversity of the calibration set:</p>
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DIVERSE}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{DIVERSE}(\theta_{Q},X^{(T)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j,i\neq j}\max(0,abs({\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(i)}}^{T}\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(j)})-\zeta)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ζ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j,i\neq j}\max(0,abs({\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(i)}}^{T}\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(j)})-\zeta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.9" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="abs(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">abs(.)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the absolute function; <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(j)}=\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathbf{x}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">▽</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{(j)}=\triangledown_{\theta_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{R}(\mathbf{x}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the gradient of the reconstruction loss w.r.t. <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> for sample <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is a small positive threshold. This loss encourages gradients of samples <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>) to be orthogonal when <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is close to 0. Consequently, it encourages the calibration set to be diverse.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Verification of the gradient matching on real data.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify the effectiveness of the gradient matching for the quantization process, we conduct experiments using the gradient matching on real images. Given a set of real images, we compare the performance of the quantized model calibrated over a randomly extracted subset of data and a subset of data that minimizes the gradient matching loss in (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
The results presented in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Verification of the gradient matching on real data. ‣ 3.4 Gradient matching without a validation set ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> show that the gradient matching loss (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) consistently improves the performance of the quantized model. The improvements are more significant when the number of samples is small.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>The comparative performance when quantizing the ResNet-18 model using the real data randomly selected and the real data selected by (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.3 Gradient matching ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
</figcaption>
