</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.3.3 </span>Impact of the loss factors <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an ablation study to assess the impact of the hyperparameters <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ 3.5 Final algorithm ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).
Specifically, we respectively keep one of the two variables <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed at 1, while varying the other with five different values <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,0.5,1,2,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,0.5,1,2,5</annotation></semantics></math>. The experiments are conducted with ResNet-18 with the 2/2 setting and the number of generated images is 1024 for each experiment. The results are presented in Tables <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.3.3 Impact of the loss factors 𝜆_1 and 𝜆_2 ‣ 4.3 Visualization and ablation studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 4.3.3 Impact of the loss factors 𝜆_1 and 𝜆_2 ‣ 4.3 Visualization and ablation studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
As we can see, the model’s performance degrades with larger or smaller <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we simply keep both of them at value 1.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Change in performance w.r.t. <math id="S4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ 3.5 Final algorithm ‣ 3 Method ‣ Sharpness-Aware Data Generation for Zero-shot Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">0</th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">0.5</th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">1</th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">2</th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">5</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
